DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ffwwccoonnttrrooll utility is designed to provide a way for users to access
     and control the FreeBSD FireWire subsystem.  Without options, ffwwccoonnttrrooll
     will output a list of devices that are/were connected to the bus.

     The following options are available:

     --uu _b_u_s___n_u_m
             Specify the FireWire bus number to be operated on.  The default
             is bus 0.

     --rr      Initiate bus reset.

     --tt      Show the topology map.

     --pp      Dump PHY registers.

     --cc _n_o_d_e
             Show the configuration ROM on the node.

     --dd _n_o_d_e
             Hex dump of the configuration ROM.

     --oo _n_o_d_e
             Send a link-on PHY packet to the node.

     --ss _n_o_d_e
             Write to the RESET_START register on the node.

     --ll _f_i_l_e
             Load hex dump file of the configuration ROM and parse it.

     --ff _n_o_d_e
             Force specified _n_o_d_e to be the root node on the next bus reset by
             sending a PHY config packet.  Valid values are 0 - 63.

     --gg _g_a_p___c_o_u_n_t
             Broadcast new _g_a_p___c_o_u_n_t by sending a PHY_config packet.  By de‐
             fault this value is 63 on all nodes.  Valid values are 0 - 63.

     --ii _p_r_i___r_e_q
             Set the PRIORITY_BUDGET register on all supported nodes.

     --MM _m_o_d_e
             Explicitly specify either _d_v or _m_p_e_g mode for the incoming
             stream.  Only meaningful in case of and must precede the --RR op‐
             tion.  If not specified, the program will try to guess.  In case
             of “format 0x20” error, try to force the “mpeg” mode.

     --RR _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e
             Receive DV or MPEG TS stream and dump it to a file.  Use ^C to
             stop the receiving.  Some DV cameras seem not to send the stream
             if a bus manager exists.  If it is impossible to get the stream,
             try the following commands:

                   sysctl hw.firewire.try_bmr=0
                   fwcontrol -r

             The resulting file contains raw DV data excluding isochronous
             header and CIP header.  It can be handled by lliibbddvv in the FreeBSD
             Ports Collection.  Resulting MPEG TS stream can be played and
             sent over a network using the VideoLAN vvllcc tool in the FreeBSD
             Ports Collection.  The stream can be piped directly to vvllcc,, see
             _E_X_A_M_P_L_E_S.

     --SS _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e
             Send a DV file as isochronous stream.

     --mm _E_U_I_6_4 | _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e
             Set default fwmem target.  Hostname will be converted to EUI64
             using eui64(5).

FFIILLEESS
